11.8:
Put on, O Yerushalayim, your esteemed garments;
Make ready your qodesh robe;
For 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 has spoken good concerning Yisra’ĕl, forever and ever.

11.9:
Let the Meleḵ 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 do what He has spoken concerning Yisra’ĕl and Yerushalayim;
Let the Meleḵ 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 raise up Yisra’ĕl by His esteemed name.
The mercy of the Meleḵ 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 be upon Yisra’ĕl forever and ever.

12.4:
To involve households in warfare by means of slanderous lips.
May Elohim remove far from the innocent the lips of transgressors by bringing them to want;
And may the bones of slanderers be scattered far away from those who fear 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄!

12.7:
The deliverance of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 be upon Yisra’ĕl His servant forever;
And let the sinners perish together at the presence of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄;
But let 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄’s pious ones inherit the promises of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄.

13.9:
For 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 spares His pious ones,
And blots out their errors by His discipline.
For the life of the righteous shall be forever;

14.3:
Their planting is rooted forever;
They shall not be plucked up all the days of the shamayim:
For the portion and the inheritance of Elohim is Yisra’ĕl.

14.4:
But not so are the sinners and transgressors,
Who love the brief day spent in companionship with their sin;
Their delight is in fleeting corruption,

15.9:
For they shall flee away from the pious as men pursued in war;
But they shall pursue sinners and overtake them,
And those who do lawlessness shall not escape the judgment of Elohim;
As by enemies experienced in war shall they be overtaken,

15.15:
But those who fear 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 shall find mercy in it,
And shall live by the compassion of their Elohim;
But sinners shall perish forever.

17.6:
But, for our sins, sinners rose up against us;
They assailed us and thrust us out;
What You had not promised to them, they took away from us with violence.

17.21:
For the shamayim withheld the rain from dropping upon the earth,
Springs were stopped that sprang perennially out of the deeps, that ran down from lofty mountains.
For there was none among them who did righteousness and justice;
From the chief of them to the least of them all were sinful;
He shall destroy the lawless nations with the word of his mouth;
At his rebuke nations shall flee before him,
And he shall reprove sinners for the thoughts of their heart.

17.42:
And relying upon his Elohim, throughout his days he will not stumble;
For Elohim will make him mighty by means of His Ruaḥ ha’Qodesh,
And wise by means of the spirit of understanding, with strength and righteousness.

2.14:
They mocked with their transgressions, as they themselves were accustomed to do;
In the full light of day they revealed their iniquities.
And the daughters of Yerushalayim were defiled in accordance with Your judgment,

2.30:
And I had not long to wait before Elohim showed me the insolent one
Slain on the mountains of Mitsrayim,
Esteemed of less account than the least on land and sea;

2.33:
He said: I will be master of land and sea;
And he did not recognize that it is Elohim who is great,
Mighty in His great strength.

5.11:
Birds and fish You nourish,
In that You give rain to the steppes that green grass may spring up,
So to prepare fodder in the steppe for every living thing;

8.7:
I said: They establish their ways in righteousness.
I thought upon the judgments of Elohim since the creation of the shamayim and the earth;
I held Elohim righteous in His judgments which have been from of old.

9.16:
And, now, You are our Elohim, and we the people whom You have loved:
Look and show pity, O Elohim of Yisra’ĕl, for we are Yours;
And do not remove Your mercy from us, lest they assail us.
